## Project Overview

This project explores the determinants of sleep health using a dataset of 374 individuals. It involves a comprehensive machine learning pipeline: from data cleaning and exploratory analysis (EDA) to building predictive models using **Regularized Regression (Elastic Net)** and **Random Forest Classifiers**.

### 🏆 Academic Achievement

Submitted as a summative assessment for **DS202A: Data Science for Social Scientists** at the **London School of Economics (LSE)**. - **Score:** 80/100 (High Distinction / First Class Honours equivalent). - **Feedback:** Highly praised for the rigorous methodological approach, particularly in handling non-normal distributions (Yeo-Johnson transformation) and ethical reflection.

